	)
	(text_box "CLK1 IS THE NULL-CHANNEL SOURCE.\nSet it to exactly 10.000000 MHz and patch this SMA to channel 13 with a short coax.  Round 28: CLK1\nruns from PLLB in INTEGER mode (25 MHz x 32 = 800 MHz, MultiSynth 80) and the helper from PLLA.\nSame TCXO, so the beat is exactly 1234.4 Hz; two PLLs, so what channel 13 reports is the front end\nplus the PLLs' uncorrelated noise - an UPPER BOUND on the floor, not 'noiseless' as earlier rounds\nsaid.  (CLK1 off PLLA would need MultiSynth 80.0099, the fractional mode the helper was steered away\nfrom.)  A cable rather than a jumper keeps every channel tile identical and puts a real connector in\nthe loop, which is the honest thing to measure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400.0500 45.7200 0)
		(size 170.1800 24.1300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d2817b4-39d2-2f87-2179-d5e301fcfb84")
	)
